55,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Candidate A seems safest. It's local, likely not too heavy, and garments can be protected.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Candidate A and C both offer the ""human presence"" visitors want. But C requires a conservation bench.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, the lab is too full for C! We can't have more work there. A is perfect for the history volunteers!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"A is local, so no shipping delays. D has too many powered parts, and B has too many loans.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,I agree. A minimizes transport costs and mount charges if the craftspeople provide their own tools.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I feel more comfortable with A. It doesn't seem to risk the floor or the evening hire.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"If the lab is the bottleneck, C is out. A provides the interaction people crave.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Rin,,Let's go with A! It's the most fun and the staff can actually do it!,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"A is the way to go. No stress at the door, no broken motors.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,The logic is sound. A is the most fiscally and operationally responsible choice.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
